title: "frame-system: require explicit weight info in default configs"

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      `frame_system::Config::SystemWeightInfo` and
      `frame_system::Config::ExtensionsWeightInfo` no longer have a default in
      the `DefaultConfig` provided by `TestDefaultConfig`, `SolochainDefaultConfig`
      and `ParaChainDefaultConfig` (they are now marked `#[pallet::no_default]`).

      Previously these types silently defaulted to `()`, which resolves to the
      Substrate reference weights benchmarked for a different runtime. This is
      almost never correct outside of testing and was an error-prone default
      (see issue #10758).

      Runtimes deriving their `frame_system::Config` via `#[derive_impl(...)]`
      from one of these default configs must now set both types explicitly, e.g.:

      ```rust
      impl frame_system::Config for Runtime {
          // Use the weights benchmarked for your runtime instead of `()` where possible.
          type SystemWeightInfo = ();
          type ExtensionsWeightInfo = ();
          // ...
      }
      ```

